    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "144e05d5347e9ff98598f627daf924e3245b38c616a573a85762cc6bc3ba0aca",
      "text": "Day 4 · Breakfast at the hotel. Transfer to the airport with your driver and flight to Foz do Iguaçu, where your driver meets you for the transfer to the hotel.\n\nFoz do Iguaçu lies at the tri-border of Brazil, Paraguay and Argentina; once a frontier military post, it grew with construction and tourism. The falls take their name from an Indigenous word meaning “great waters”. Formed by the Iguaçu River, they comprise 275 individual cascades surrounded by the pristine forest of Iguaçu National Park, home to some 2,000 plant species and 400 bird species, including parrots and toucans. The most powerful of all is the Devil’s Throat.",
